`src/blog/people/drafts/Nate-Bargatze.md`, in perspective-jury mode against `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Nate-Bargatze/2026-08-25_020002` (synthesis verified against the frozen SHA `5551c59a…`, which still matched the working file).

**All 12 P0 items fixed, all 15 accepted P1s applied**, plus P2-02 and P2-06.

The dominant problem wasn't prose, it was that a piece arguing this man notices arithmetic had six wrong numbers and three misattributed quotes. The repairs that mattered most:

- **The closer was self-refuting.** It put the park "on the ground where he watched the trick get done"; the same article says a mall is there. Now "in the city where."
- **The cold open's showcase coincidence doesn't exist.** 19,365 tickets decomposes to 19 years + 365 days, but he started in 2002 — that's twenty-one years, and the draft says 2002 itself. Cut the arithmetic; his own "which is 20 years" now sits directly against "I'm not even into numbers," which is the actual thesis.
- **The tour clause was wrong three ways and omitted the Guinness record** set nine days before the draft date. Five of six perspectives caught the omission independently. It's now in the intro as fact and weighed in the counterargument section.
- **Two quotes were credited to an aggregator that never conducted an interview**, one off by a year, and the closer's load-bearing quote had "try to" silently dropped. Re-attributed to The Christian Post and NYT/Marchese; "try to" restored.
- **The stated Type 9 core fear was wrong**, inside the sentence accusing everyone else of getting the mechanism backwards. Now matches `enneagram-type-9.md`, and naming the gut center finally gives the anger closer its engine.
- **Two invented-interiority and never-in-his-life problems** removed: the Grammy inner-thought contradicted his own posted account two lines above it.

